# The gcp profile: hosting on Google Cloud Run for an app on the vite-react-tanstack profile.
# One service serves the built client and answers /api/* with a Hono app on Node, and
# OpenTofu describes the GCP project around it. Opt in with `gcp` in the project's
# .template-profiles, after vite-react-tanstack. Same syntax as .template/manifest, but every
# path is read from .template/profiles/gcp/ rather than from the template's root.
#
# Most of what it manages is in .devtools/host/, which the vite-react-tanstack profile's
# shared configs load when it exists: its Vite plugin and server build, its Vitest project,
# its ESLint rules and its make targets. Nothing in the project's own config files names the
# host, so a project lists one hosting profile at a time. Moving to another is a swap of
# names in .template-profiles, `rm -r .devtools/host`, and a sync.
#
# Per project, and not listed: Dockerfile, .gcloudignore, everything under server/ and
# infra/, and the job in release.yml that deploys a release (deploy.yml shows it).
# `node .devtools/scripts/gen.mjs host` writes a first version of them and installs the
# packages; `gen.mjs app` does the same when the profile is there first.

file  .devtools/host/host.mk
file  .devtools/host/vite.ts
file  .devtools/host/server.ts
file  .devtools/host/vitest.ts
file  .devtools/host/eslint.js
file  .devtools/host/scaffold.mjs
file  .github/workflows/deploy.yml

block mise.toml               gcp
block lefthook.yml            gcp
block .gitignore              gcp
block .editorconfig           gcp
block .github/dependabot.yml  gcp
block AGENTS.md               gcp
